  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "opening",
      "arabic_text": "وَ كَتَبَ غُلَامٌ لِأَمِيرِ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ إِلَيْهِ إِنِّي قَدْ أَصَبْتُ قَوْمًا مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ زَنَادِقَةً وَ قَوْمًا مِنَ النَّصَارَى زَنَادِقَةً فَقَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "A servant wrote to Amīr al-Muʾminīn عليه السلام: “Indeed, I have encountered a group among the Muslims who are zanādiqah, and a group among the Christians who are zanādiqah.” So he said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "أَمَّا مَنْ كَانَ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ وُلِدَ عَلَى الْفِطْرَةِ ثُمَّ ارْتَدَّ فَاضْرِبْ عُنُقَهُ وَ لَا تَسْتَتِبْهُ وَ مَنْ لَمْ يُولَدْ مِنْهُمْ عَلَى الْفِطْرَةِ فَاسْتَتِبْهُ فَإِنْ تَابَ وَ إِلَّا فَاضْرِبْ عُنُقَهُ وَ أَمَّا النَّصَارَى فَمَا هُمْ عَلَيْهِ أَعْظَمُ مِنَ الزَّنْدَقَةِ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "As for the one among the Muslims who was born upon the fiṭrah and then apostatized, strike his neck and do not ask him to repent. And whoever among them was not born upon the fiṭrah, then ask him to repent; if he repents, otherwise strike his neck. And as for the Christians, what they are upon is greater than zandaqah.”
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith reports a legal ruling from Amīr al-Muʾminīn عليه السلام concerning different categories of zandaqah and apostasy. It distinguishes between one born upon fiṭrah who then apostasizes and one not born upon fiṭrah, while also stating that the belief held by the Christians is greater than zandaqah.",
      "seo_question": "What is the ruling in this hadith on Muslims accused of zandaqah and how does it distinguish between those born upon fiṭrah and others?",
      "key_terms": {
        "الْمُسْلِمِينَ": "the Muslims, referring here to those outwardly counted among Islam",
        "زَنَادِقَةً": "heretics; those described as holding zandaqah",
        "الْفِطْرَةِ": "the natural disposition, here meaning original birth upon Islam",
        "ارْتَدَّ": "apostatized; turned back from Islam",
        "تَسْتَتِبْهُ": "seek his repentance; ask him to repent",
        "تَابَ": "repented; returned from the deviant belief",
        "النَّصَارَى": "the Christians",
        "الزَّنْدَقَةِ": "zandaqah; heresy or hidden unbelief"
      }
    }
  },
